score_pct: 40.5
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config loading tests and security tests don't specifically test that parse/permission
    errors are distinguished from NotFound. The reviewer flagged deny_unknown_fields
    but not the error-swallowing pattern.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Dev implemented sanitized Display for ServerError and NotFound in error.rs\
    \ \u2014 'server error' and 'resource not found' without leaking internal details.\
    \ Reviewer verified: 'ServerError displays \"server error\" \u2014 internal details\
    \ stored in the tuple field are not exposed via Display.'"
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote header injection tests in siem_client.rs and security.rs covering\
    \ CRLF in tenant_id. Dev implemented sanitize_header_value rejecting \\r and \\\
    n. However, the finding is about using raw String instead of TenantId from axiathon-core\
    \ \u2014 the CRLF mitigation was caught but the type-safety aspect (using validated\
    \ TenantId) was not flagged."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. The reviewer did not mention this issue.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged: '[HIGH] ConfigFile does not use #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]\
    \ \u2014 unknown fields silently accepted. More critically, if someone adds token\
    \ = \"secret\" to the config file, it's silently parsed and ignored rather than\
    \ rejected with a security warning.'"
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...). The TEA wrote config tests but this specific logical flaw was not caught
    by any phase.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic
    with 'let _ = config'. Neither TEA, Dev, nor Reviewer flagged this test quality
    issue.
